          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why does my charger say my battery is defective when it works in a tool?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Often a dirty or damaged data contact. Lithium packs communicate with the charger through contacts beyond the main power terminals, so a pack can deliver power to a tool perfectly while failing to communicate with the charger. Clean all the contacts with isopropyl alcohol and try again, and cross-test on another charger."
          }
        },
