          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I charge a Ryobi battery in the cold?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No, and the charger will prevent it. Charging lithium below freezing plates metallic lithium onto the anode, causing permanent damage and a potential safety hazard. Bring the pack indoors and let it reach room temperature over one to two hours, longer for a large pack from a genuinely cold shed."
